## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js | 🚨 blocking ci red — crap ratchet exceeded on both backstopbridgemocks builders the crap check fails on head 47854b8a ci failures md ci failures full log text new 8 js unit tests test mergebot js backstopbridgemocks 9 new 8 js unit tests test mergetrigger js backstopbridgemocks 9 0 regression s 2 new over threshold 0 improvement s 0 removed error process completed with exit code 2 the resolvefailids branch added inside the github resolve pr thread mock pushes the backstopbridgemocks builder over the crap 8 threshold in both test files the pr description s all new functions ≤ 8 holds for mergebackstop js but the ratchet also covers these modified test builders fix with the repo s own precedent — a named mock builder exactly like checkrunspayload in this file gh 1200 precedent named mock builders js function resolvethreadmock opts calls return function a if opts resolvefailids indexof string a threadid 1 throw new error 422 a threadid calls threadresolves push a return in backstopbridgemocks github resolve pr thread resolvethreadmock opts calls apply the identical extraction in js unit tests test mergetrigger js its builder copy is flagged at the same threshold unit tests themselves are green verified locally 63 139 passed — this gate is the only red check |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/mergeBackstop.js | 💡 suggestion gate the ack stats fragment on ackidle out in the counted line too a important only replay zero below threshold machine threads ackidle true now appends an idle fragment to the outcome line …resolved 1 resolve failures 0 ack failures 0 suggestion nit machine thread s ack resolved without a fix wontfix 0 resolve failures 0 ack reply failures 0 0 open human thread s … cleanoutcomeline already handles this — it keeps the pure gh 1353 wording when ackidle out is true countedoutcomeline embeds ackstatsline out unconditionally so a gh 1353 only replay s log line changes shape for no information symmetric form js ack failures out ackfailures ackidle out ackstatsline out out human length optional polish — the lines are informational only no machine parser consumes them verified by grep so behavior is unaffected either way |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | js/unit-tests/test_mergeTrigger.js | 💡 suggestion dedupe the twin backstopbridgemocks builders into fixtures js unit tests test mergebot js and js unit tests test mergetrigger js carry near identical copies of backstopbridgemocks and this pr had to extend both copies with the exact same resolvefailids branch — the classic parallel edit cost of duplicated fixtures miss one copy and the two suites silently diverge in failure injection capability the repo already has a shared fixture pattern js unit tests fixtures releaseartefactsmock js is loaded via loadmodule js unit tests fixtures … makerequire in multiple suites extracting the builder there e g fixtures backstopbridgemocks js taking opts calls and returning the mock bag ends the parallel edits — and doing it together with the resolve fail extraction from the blocking thread drops both copies below the crap ratchet in one move the two copies do differ today mergebot s also mocks github search issues for calls debtsearches — parameterize that one difference rather than merging blindly |
| F4 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/mergeBackstop.js | 💡 suggestion document the none severity fallthrough onto the wontfix ack path the ack path covers everything below rank important — including a machine thread whose body carries no recognizable severity marker reviewverdicts threadseverity returns none for it and findingregistry severityclassof falls back to suggestion findingregistry js 225 — nit also maps through the fallback so it lands here deliberately net behavior a marker less machine owned thread is now auto resolved at merge time with a public wontfix below gating threshold — epic invariant gh 1370 ack — under gh 1353 it was left untouched the triage path s business confirm this is intended for what it s worth the alternative is a deadlock holding the merge on an unresolvable classification would never converge so ack path is the only terminal outcome for such threads — but that reasoning and the none → ack fallthrough deserves one line in the classifythreads doc comment so a later audit reading the digest ack trail understands why a marker less thread closed as wontfix rather than being a misclassification |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

